WEBVTT

00:00.740 --> 00:02.850
At the dawn of the Seika era,

00:02.850 --> 00:06.060
in order to regulate unwanted messages that presented a bad influence to society,

00:06.060 --> 00:08.460
the Media Cleansing Act was passed.

00:09.420 --> 00:12.780
The libraries armed themselves in order to protect freedom of expression

00:12.780 --> 00:15.410
from the extreme censorship of the Media Cleansing Committee.

00:15.910 --> 00:19.420
The conflict between the two continued to escalate.

00:20.100 --> 00:25.800
In the 31st year of Seika, a lone girl plunged herself into the middle of that conflict.

00:33.030 --> 00:37.630
usu murasaki hirogaru

00:33.030 --> 00:37.630
The faint purple spreads across the sky

00:37.630 --> 00:45.610
orenji iro ni kawaru mado no soto

00:37.630 --> 00:45.610
The color changes to orange outside the window

00:45.610 --> 00:49.660
yoru wa mou bai bai

00:45.610 --> 00:49.660
The night's already "bye-bye"

00:50.210 --> 00:55.900
tada kirei na mono wo kirei to

00:50.210 --> 00:55.900
I just want to be someone who

00:55.900 --> 01:00.460
ieru atashi de itai

00:55.900 --> 01:00.460
calls beautiful things beautiful

01:00.460 --> 01:06.800
ima wa dokidoki shitai no

01:00.460 --> 01:06.800
I want to get excited for it!

01:07.330 --> 01:11.860
fumidashichae tomaranai

01:07.330 --> 01:11.860
So I step out, unstoppable

01:11.860 --> 01:16.450
zenbu te ni hairi sou de

01:11.860 --> 01:16.450
And take everything into my own hands

01:16.940 --> 01:21.050
sono saki de aitai

01:16.940 --> 01:21.050
Beyond there, I want to meet

01:21.050 --> 01:27.040
mita koto no nai atashi

01:21.050 --> 01:27.040
the new self that I've never seen

01:27.510 --> 01:32.160
sayonara daisuki na machi

01:27.510 --> 01:32.160
Farewell, my beloved town

01:32.160 --> 01:36.710
atashi mo ganbatte miru yo

01:32.160 --> 01:36.710
I'll try to do my best

01:36.710 --> 01:44.270
kono sora no tsuzuku basho de

01:36.710 --> 01:44.270
somewhere under the same sky

01:49.690 --> 01:52.530
What's with the sulky face?

01:52.700 --> 01:55.490
Do you still have something against me?

01:56.290 --> 01:57.730
Do you...

01:58.520 --> 02:00.250
want to go out with me?

02:07.910 --> 02:12.360
Situation 03

02:07.910 --> 02:12.360
Battle of Odawara

02:12.840 --> 02:16.010
So, how did you respond?

02:16.240 --> 02:19.760
I told him to let me think it over for a while...

02:20.350 --> 02:22.080
You bum.

02:22.080 --> 02:24.050
But!

02:24.050 --> 02:26.820
It's the first time anyone's asked me out.

02:26.820 --> 02:28.150
First time?!

02:28.150 --> 02:30.750
Well, I understand how you feel...

02:31.270 --> 02:35.140
So, is dating him an option?

02:36.850 --> 02:44.470
He's serious, he's got good grades, he's handsome, <i>and</i> he's taller than you.

02:44.870 --> 02:47.840
Kasahara Iku

02:44.890 --> 02:49.210
By most people's standards, he's infinitely close to perfection.

02:45.020 --> 02:46.180
Defence Force, Library Task Force

02:46.180 --> 02:46.860
Rank: Librarian First Class

02:46.860 --> 02:47.840
Hot-headed Idiot

02:49.210 --> 02:52.700
On top of that, his father is the chairman of the Library Commission.

02:49.280 --> 02:52.210
Shibasaki Asako

02:49.430 --> 02:50.590
First Musashino Library Administration

02:50.590 --> 02:51.270
Rank: Librarian First Class

02:51.270 --> 02:52.210
Informant

02:53.420 --> 02:55.100
You didn't know?!

02:55.100 --> 02:56.820
You're too ignorant.

02:56.820 --> 03:02.600
But dating him for those reasons feels a bit wrong...

03:02.600 --> 03:05.840
If it's not with someone I like...

03:07.250 --> 03:08.920
A virgin!

03:08.920 --> 03:11.550
We have a virgin here!

03:10.170 --> 03:10.870
Shut up!

03:10.870 --> 03:11.740
Don't make fun of the situation!

03:11.740 --> 03:14.070
Do you have someone you like then?

03:14.070 --> 03:15.500
L...

03:16.680 --> 03:18.820
Yes, someone you like.

03:21.260 --> 03:22.720
Not really.

03:22.720 --> 03:25.530
Then why not!

03:25.530 --> 03:29.020
I'm really curious how you two would turn out.

03:29.020 --> 03:32.200
I don't want to do this to indulge your curiosity!

03:32.880 --> 03:37.720
All we need is the suspect's library check-out record.

03:37.720 --> 03:45.450
It is our duty to protect the library user's privacy in accordance with Article 32 of the Library Act.

03:45.450 --> 03:51.700
Our library cannot break the law just to help the police.

03:51.700 --> 03:54.810
But it can be used to help make the suspect confess!

03:54.810 --> 03:56.850
The public will understand too!

03:57.390 --> 04:01.900
I believe the law must not be bent just to suit the situation.

04:04.390 --> 04:05.340
What's wrong with him?!

04:05.340 --> 04:07.350
Three people have been killed already.

04:07.350 --> 04:08.670
What an attitude...

04:08.670 --> 04:10.060
Stop it.

04:10.060 --> 04:13.820
We're the ones asking them to disclose information unlawfully.

04:14.320 --> 04:16.910
We didn't have a chance to start with.

04:17.370 --> 04:19.140
The Hino Nightmare.

04:19.470 --> 04:21.490
You've at least heard of it, haven't you?

04:21.800 --> 04:23.540
It happened twenty years ago.

04:23.540 --> 04:27.340
Yes. I was in grade school then.

04:27.340 --> 04:33.050
That man, Inamine Kazuichi, is one of the survivors.

04:37.990 --> 04:41.750
It was said that the delayed police response had been due to reports

04:41.750 --> 04:45.270
that erroneously attributed the attack to the Media Cleansing Force.

04:53.060 --> 04:57.370
You claim to protect public order, and you kill people to do it?!

05:18.280 --> 05:20.360
There were 12 casualties.

05:20.590 --> 05:23.340
He lost his wife and his right leg.

05:23.930 --> 05:27.080
The attackers were too well-armed.

05:27.430 --> 05:31.280
There were suspicions that the Media Cleansing Force intervened,

05:31.280 --> 05:34.970
but the investigation was stopped without producing a clear result.

05:36.310 --> 05:41.990
Since that day, the Library Forces armed themselves in self-defense.

05:44.370 --> 05:46.890
He's still at the forefront of that battle.

05:50.040 --> 05:56.500
The former CEO and current Chief Advisor of the Nobeyama Group, the largest trading company in the country,

05:56.500 --> 06:00.710
Nobeyama Sohachi, has passed away earlier this morning in a hospital in Odawara.

06:00.710 --> 06:03.020
According to a press release by the group of doctors...

06:20.870 --> 06:23.960
Why would you sit next to me?!

06:23.960 --> 06:26.210
Sense my discomfort!

06:26.380 --> 06:31.920
The Museum of Information History that Mr. Nobeyama operated is being closed.

06:33.010 --> 06:38.180
With that, a decision was made that the Kanto Library Force will receive ownership of the books.

06:34.760 --> 06:37.670
Genda Ryusuke

06:34.910 --> 06:35.980
Defense Force, Captain

06:35.980 --> 06:36.820
Rank: Library Supervisor Third Class

06:36.820 --> 06:37.670
Middle-aged Wrangler

06:40.110 --> 06:46.520
It's a private library in Odawara that collected historic publications regarding the Media Cleansing Committee.

06:40.250 --> 06:43.160
Dojo Atsushi

06:40.400 --> 06:41.470
Defense Force, Library Task Force

06:41.470 --> 06:42.310
Rank: Library Office Second Class

06:42.310 --> 06:43.160
Angry Shorty

06:47.230 --> 06:49.030
Unbelievable.

06:48.350 --> 06:51.260
Tezuka Hikaru

06:48.500 --> 06:49.570
Defense Force, Library Task Force

06:49.030 --> 06:54.070
It's unthinkable for a Library Force member not to know about the Museum of Information History.

06:49.570 --> 06:50.410
Rank: Librarian First Class

06:50.410 --> 06:51.260
Stubborn Young Man

06:54.070 --> 06:57.690
But they don't even teach that in the lectures!

06:57.690 --> 07:01.530
It was left untouched because it was privately owned.

07:02.390 --> 07:06.720
But to the Cleansing Committee, the place is full of documents they want to eliminate.

07:07.200 --> 07:13.330
We're expecting interference by the Media Cleansing Force and other supporting groups on the day of the hand-off.

07:14.000 --> 07:18.090
The closing of the museum is set on the day of Mr. Nobeyama's funeral.

07:18.090 --> 07:20.760
The book transfer will be done on that day as well.

07:21.040 --> 07:23.710
The entire Task Force will join the operation.

07:23.710 --> 07:26.780
We will move into the site the day before.

07:26.990 --> 07:31.100
Members of the Kanagawa Prefecture Defense Force will join us there as well.

07:31.740 --> 07:35.980
The books will be transported by air using a helicopter.

07:35.980 --> 07:40.500
The first flight will take off from the museum at 0900.

07:40.500 --> 07:45.380
The Defense Forces will work on securing the perimeter until the hand-off is complete.

07:45.990 --> 07:53.610
Also, LFC Kasahara will escort Commander Inamine, who will attend the funeral.

07:53.770 --> 07:55.330
That's all.

07:55.430 --> 07:57.340
Just me?

07:58.750 --> 08:00.700
What's going on?!

08:00.700 --> 08:02.990
Tell me the reason!

08:03.340 --> 08:06.130
Escorting key personnel is also one of the Task Force's duties,

08:06.130 --> 08:08.100
so it's nothing special to send some of us to do it.

08:08.680 --> 08:11.440
But why me alone?!

08:12.210 --> 08:14.380
It's to give you more experience.

08:14.510 --> 08:17.450
Then why is Tezuka not included?

08:17.450 --> 08:20.010
Does he not need the experience?!

08:20.290 --> 08:22.440
Don't dupe me!

08:22.840 --> 08:23.990
Fine.

08:24.770 --> 08:27.560
I'll tell you since you seem to be able to handle it.

08:28.610 --> 08:32.000
I judged that you won't be of any use.

08:34.830 --> 08:36.290
Are you satisfied?

08:40.770 --> 08:46.040
Instructor Dojo, you don't trust me?

08:48.000 --> 08:51.340
Why do I do this when I already know the result?

08:52.210 --> 08:56.410
Have you done anything that inspires trust?

09:12.060 --> 09:15.030
You look like an abandoned dog.

09:15.030 --> 09:17.550
I'll never want him as my owner.

09:17.550 --> 09:20.590
And who's that owner?

09:25.560 --> 09:29.690
Are you serious about your comment that Kasahara is of no use?

09:30.090 --> 09:33.020
Sure, she's an ignorant idiot,

09:33.020 --> 09:35.570
but her overall training results are not much different from mine!

09:35.570 --> 09:39.820
It's hard to believe I'm hearing this from you.

09:40.790 --> 09:44.610
Are you, as an instructor, using a double standard?!

09:45.950 --> 09:47.440
Yeah...

09:49.370 --> 09:52.410
I hear they're getting nervous down in Odawara.

09:52.410 --> 09:56.710
In the worst case scenario, it may become an incident even worse than the Hino Nightmare.

09:56.890 --> 09:58.920
Is it that bad?

09:58.920 --> 10:02.210
I heard that the entire Defense Force will be armed with submachine guns.

10:02.210 --> 10:06.590
And I've never heard of something as extreme as the deployment of the entire Task Force.

10:07.340 --> 10:11.870
But I'm not included in that <i>entire</i> Task Force.

10:11.870 --> 10:16.360
For this mission from which some of us may never come back!

10:17.120 --> 10:19.070
Why was I...?

10:19.600 --> 10:22.690
Hey, stop sulking.

10:23.300 --> 10:24.550
Don't worry.

10:24.550 --> 10:26.940
The Library Force is different from twenty years ago.

10:26.940 --> 10:28.980
We have adequate equipment and training.

10:28.980 --> 10:33.800
The public acknowledges us as people with more actual combat experience than the police or the JSDF.

10:34.090 --> 10:37.250
And I'm a member of it too!

10:37.250 --> 10:37.970
And still...

10:37.970 --> 10:39.880
Enough. Don't you get it?

10:40.690 --> 10:44.460
They excluded you because you're a naive baby who doesn't acknowledge her immaturity.

10:47.390 --> 10:49.440
I'm sorry, I said too much.

10:49.560 --> 10:53.280
Captain Genda was originally going to include you.

10:53.280 --> 10:56.810
The exclusion is a selfish act by Instructor Dojo.

10:57.540 --> 10:59.150
What do you mean?

10:59.310 --> 11:01.850
I'm sorry for acting out of place.

11:01.850 --> 11:03.670
Excuse me now.

11:05.670 --> 11:08.850
You can't blame anyone no matter what you're told this time.

11:08.850 --> 11:13.200
Kasahara-san must deal with her own personal problems.

11:09.030 --> 11:11.940
Komaki Mikihisa

11:09.180 --> 11:10.250
Defense Force, Library Task Force

11:10.250 --> 11:11.090
Rank: Library Office Second Class

11:11.090 --> 11:11.940
Smiling Logician

11:13.200 --> 11:18.150
It's wrong for you to stick your head in and get everyone else involved.

11:20.310 --> 11:26.760
You are a disobedient child who hasn't told her parents about being assigned to a combat-oriented group.

11:31.290 --> 11:34.170
I didn't ask for help.

11:34.170 --> 11:36.340
Like I said, it was selfish on his part.

11:36.340 --> 11:37.970
He's doing you a favor.

11:37.970 --> 11:40.460
I don't want such a favor!

11:40.460 --> 11:42.900
Who made him do it?

11:48.120 --> 11:54.520
It's because I couldn't deal with my own problems, isn't it?

11:55.790 --> 11:57.820
So you do get it.

11:59.820 --> 12:05.450
A person who can't deal with her own problems can't ask to be trusted.

12:08.290 --> 12:09.730
Shibasaki,

12:10.440 --> 12:12.710
help me train for my escort duty.

12:18.590 --> 12:21.140
You're really serious about this.

12:22.290 --> 12:25.400
They know it will be a fierce one too.

12:26.720 --> 12:29.060
What about the first female Task Force member?

12:29.060 --> 12:32.070
She's on something else for a reason.

12:32.960 --> 12:35.020
There she is.

12:35.020 --> 12:37.030
Kasahara!

12:49.290 --> 12:54.850
Pictures of her cannot be published for a reason, so please spare her.

12:55.040 --> 12:56.630
Sorry for that.

12:56.630 --> 12:58.840
What a waste of a good picture.

12:58.840 --> 13:01.680
Captain, who might that be?

13:01.680 --> 13:03.740
Sorry for not introducing myself sooner.

13:03.870 --> 13:07.060
I'm Orikuchi Maki from Sesou Publishing.

13:07.060 --> 13:10.570
We've know each other since college.

13:10.570 --> 13:14.020
She requested to cover this case.

13:14.020 --> 13:18.700
As a member of the mass media, I believe this is an event we cannot ignore.

13:18.700 --> 13:22.360
I intend to write a powerful article that will live up to your actions.

13:22.360 --> 13:23.960
Please look forward to it.

13:40.760 --> 13:42.150
You're leaving now?

13:42.150 --> 13:43.520
Yeah.

13:43.860 --> 13:45.850
Take care of yourself.

13:54.240 --> 13:55.660
Kasahara,

13:57.560 --> 14:00.700
when will you answer my question from the other night?

14:07.400 --> 14:10.890
I'll tell you next time.

14:11.070 --> 14:12.420
Next time?

14:13.190 --> 14:14.290
Yeah.

14:15.410 --> 14:16.860
Next time.

14:28.400 --> 14:32.860
Odawa Museum of Information History
Closing Day 9:00 a.m.

14:34.770 --> 14:36.530
Here they come.

14:37.130 --> 14:40.260
This is the Cleansing Force on behalf of the Media Cleansing Committee.

14:37.130 --> 14:39.140
Try not to hit anyone.

14:39.140 --> 14:42.240
Any casualties will only escalate the battle.

14:40.260 --> 14:43.410
As of this moment, and as stated in notice #7726,

14:42.240 --> 14:45.080
Do you think they'll go that easily?

14:43.410 --> 14:46.680
we are executing the censorship of the documents on behalf of the chairman of the committee, Onodera Shigeru,

14:45.080 --> 14:48.710
The ground troops will have to take the blow if we anger them.

14:46.680 --> 14:50.170
in accordance with Article 3 of the Media Cleansing Act.

14:50.240 --> 14:52.560
I'm not expecting great accuracy from you.

14:51.120 --> 14:55.220
The Kanto Library Force is to disarm itself and surrender immediately!

14:52.560 --> 14:54.840
We just need to pressure them.

14:55.220 --> 14:56.630
Roger.

14:57.430 --> 15:00.880
The Kanto Library Force is executing their right to protect literature

15:00.880 --> 15:06.590
in accordance with Article 4 of the Library Act, and Article 34 of the Library Freedom Act.

15:06.590 --> 15:09.100
If you want to censor these books...

15:09.100 --> 15:11.360
come and get them!

15:11.590 --> 15:13.730
I'll be counting on you today.

15:13.730 --> 15:14.850
Yes, Sir.

15:14.850 --> 15:17.490
I will do my job properly.

15:41.150 --> 15:43.760
Isn't the helicopter going up yet?

15:44.730 --> 15:45.880
Snipers?!

15:45.880 --> 15:46.680
Damn it!

15:51.240 --> 15:52.400
There he is!

15:54.580 --> 15:55.920
Yes!

16:03.310 --> 16:05.130
The helicopter has left the perimeter.

16:05.130 --> 16:06.400
No damage taken.

16:06.400 --> 16:08.140
How many seriously injured are there?

16:08.140 --> 16:10.480
13 cases reported.

16:10.480 --> 16:12.640
We'll carry them in the second helicopter.

16:12.640 --> 16:15.880
There are some who may not survive with first aid alone.

16:18.290 --> 16:21.040
We will provide our press helicopter.

16:22.700 --> 16:26.540
Our battle is to write about the fighting men like you.

16:26.540 --> 16:30.410
We kept one on standby just in case something like this happened.

16:31.490 --> 16:33.130
Sorry about that.

16:33.130 --> 16:34.570
Yes, please.

16:45.020 --> 16:48.050
Frontline ground troops, retreat to the building interior.

16:48.350 --> 16:49.580
Roger.

16:51.240 --> 16:52.080
Go!

16:52.080 --> 16:55.460
Two hours have passed since the battle started.

16:56.830 --> 16:58.590
Komaki! We're retreating!

17:05.130 --> 17:06.260
Komaki!

17:07.090 --> 17:08.470
We're retrieving an injured!

17:08.470 --> 17:10.560
Back us up!

17:13.360 --> 17:20.570
The Kanto Library Force protects the containers that are filled with the entire history of censorship.

17:21.620 --> 17:24.970
The Media Cleansing Force does not hesitate to shed blood over the censorship.

17:24.970 --> 17:30.130
The list of injured continues to increase without giving us any time to think about the validity of it all.

17:30.130 --> 17:33.550
And then the second helicopter arrived.

17:33.550 --> 17:34.840
The helicopter is closing in.

17:34.840 --> 17:38.800
Snipers, switch to submachine guns and back up the landing.

17:38.800 --> 17:42.720
Concentrate on the troops that are in the direction from which the helicopter is approaching.

17:43.230 --> 17:44.660
Put up a barrage!

17:59.960 --> 18:01.150
Tezuka!

18:21.720 --> 18:23.260
All units inside the building,

18:23.260 --> 18:25.040
the helicopter is preparing to take off.

18:25.040 --> 18:26.330
It won't take long.

18:26.330 --> 18:27.620
Hang in there!

18:27.620 --> 18:29.280
We're at our limit!

18:29.280 --> 18:30.630
No more!

18:30.630 --> 18:32.640
He's at his limit too!

18:32.640 --> 18:34.440
Take him to the hospital ASAP!

18:34.440 --> 18:35.910
But...

18:39.000 --> 18:40.310
Hurry!

18:40.310 --> 18:41.400
Thanks...

18:51.650 --> 18:53.400
Hang in there!

18:53.400 --> 18:55.870
Once this one takes off, it'll be our victory!

19:15.500 --> 19:17.400
Operation complete.

19:17.400 --> 19:19.060
Patch me through to the PA system.

19:20.460 --> 19:23.940
Notice from the Kanto Library Force to the Media Cleansing Force.

19:23.940 --> 19:29.530
The Library Force is abandoning all the remaining publications in the building as of 1140.

19:30.210 --> 19:34.450
Use telephone extension 03 to respond.

19:39.330 --> 19:42.190
From the Media Cleansing Force to the Kanto Library Force.

19:42.190 --> 19:45.560
Leave the building by 1210.

19:45.560 --> 19:49.170
We will not permit reentry to the building.

19:49.170 --> 19:50.590
Over.

19:51.900 --> 19:53.570
What's this about?

19:53.570 --> 19:56.480
Isn't there one more container?

19:56.710 --> 19:59.040
That one was made to be abandoned.

19:59.040 --> 20:02.770
It has magazines and books that the Library Force has backups for.

20:03.530 --> 20:06.220
They can't go home empty-handed either.

20:06.220 --> 20:07.810
This is where we draw the line.

20:09.180 --> 20:12.280
It must not be easy to be the righteous hero, with all this formality.

20:12.430 --> 20:13.580
Yeah.

20:13.580 --> 20:15.230
Now you see.

20:16.810 --> 20:19.760
All Cleansing Force members have retreated away from the building.

20:19.760 --> 20:20.970
Good work.

20:20.970 --> 20:26.170
Dojo, Komaki, the squad member you retrieved has been safely transported.

20:26.170 --> 20:27.720
That's good to hear.

20:29.350 --> 20:30.880
Great.

20:43.680 --> 20:45.400
All units,

20:45.510 --> 20:49.070
suspicious individuals have entered Mr. Nobeyama's funeral site.

20:49.700 --> 20:52.110
Commander Inamine is under attack.

20:52.110 --> 20:54.320
All units, retreat immediately!

20:54.320 --> 20:55.670
We're returning to base!

20:55.670 --> 20:57.700
Kasahara!

21:06.690 --> 21:10.030
nani ka ga kawaru kigashita

21:06.690 --> 21:10.030
I had a feeling something was about to change

21:10.030 --> 21:13.410
nani mo kawaranu asa ni

21:10.030 --> 21:13.410
on this very ordinary morning

21:13.410 --> 21:18.420
itsu mo yori sukoshi ii mezamedatta

21:13.410 --> 21:18.420
I woke up feeling a little better than usual

21:20.080 --> 21:26.760
hito sashiyubi de sashimesu no wa mirai

21:20.080 --> 21:26.760
My index finger points out to the future

21:26.760 --> 21:36.430
kimi no te no hira ga fureru tabi ni afuru omoi

21:26.760 --> 21:36.430
My thoughts overflow each time I touch your palm

21:36.880 --> 21:40.410
ch-ch-ch-changes saa kawatteku

21:36.880 --> 21:40.410
Changes, yeah. I'm changing.

21:40.410 --> 21:43.730
sayonara furui jibun

21:40.410 --> 21:43.730
Goodbye my old self

21:43.730 --> 21:50.260
shingenjitsu atarashii nani ka ga matteru

